{"t": 1794115861.3945832, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*PaymentGatewayErrors / checkout \u2014 root cause found, fix ready*\n\n\u2022 Symptom: gateway 4xx rate 38% since 07:41 UTC; charges rejected with 400 `invalid_amount`.\n\u2022 Cause: payment gateway switched to API 2026-11 (strict amounts) at 07:41 UTC. It now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents). `checkout/gateway.py` still sent a decimal major-unit float (e.g. `{\"amount\": 12.34}`), so every charge is rejected.\n\u2022 Fix: `charge_payload()` now converts EUR to integer cents (`12.34 -> 1234`) using Decimal + ROUND_HALF_UP to avoid float artifacts (e.g. 4.35 must not become 434). Verified locally across edge cases; no other callers or tests in the repo.\n\u2022 Impact: all checkout charges fail until deployed. No data corruption \u2014 rejections are pre-authorization.\n\u2022 Next: deploy `checkout` to prod-eu-1, then watch 4xx rate on `{app=\"checkout\"}` and confirm charges succeed. Rollback is a plain revert if needed.\n\u2022 Open question: rounding policy for sub-cent amounts is not documented anywhere I could find; current behaviour is half-up on cents. Worth confirming with the gateway provider if sub-cent totals can occur."}, "ok": true}
